","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Snowplow’s mobile trackers send at most 25 events and 40,000 bytes in a request by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and an event larger than that in a request of its own. A collector refuses a body over 2 MB","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with 413, and a request larger than its stream takes (192,000 bytes on SQS, 1 MB on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Kinesis, by default) becomes a failed event though the collector answers 200. So an event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of up to 150,000 bytes of JSON is sent alone, within the smallest of those, and a larger one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is left out as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError\/oversized(byteCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}],"title":"BatchEncoder","abstract":[{"text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":" sends.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BatchEncoder"}]},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"iden